"""Make a standalone native photo appraisal with a pixel-difference filter."""
import json
import base64
from pathlib import Path

ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]
OUT=ROOT/'build/n64-sidewinder-photography'

HTML=r'''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
<title>Sidewinder — terrain appraisal</title><style>
:root{color-scheme:dark;font:16px/1.55 system-ui;background:#10151c;color:#e9edf4}body{max-width:1250px;margin:auto;padding:28px}h1{font-size:34px;margin:0}h2{font-size:23px}p{max-width:90ch;color:#bcc8d7}button,select,input{font:inherit}button,select{background:#202d3c;color:white;border:1px solid #52677f;border-radius:7px;padding:7px 12px}button.active{background:#116e9c;border-color:#58c9ff}.tools{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:12px;align-items:center;margin:15px 0}input[type=range]{width:150px;accent-color:#62d2ff}.frame{position:relative;width:100%;max-width:960px;aspect-ratio:4/3;background:#000;overflow:hidden}.frame img,.frame canvas{position:absolute;inset:0;width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:fill}.frame .top{clip-path:inset(0 50% 0 0)}.divider{position:absolute;top:0;bottom:0;left:50%;width:2px;background:#62d2ff}.hidden{display:none!important}pre{white-space:pre-wrap;font:13px/1.5 ui-monospace;background:#17212d;padding:14px;border-radius:8px;color:#c8d8e8}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;margin:15px 0}td,th{padding:9px 12px;border-bottom:1px solid #354458;text-align:left}th{color:#7dd6fd}a{color:#7dd6fd}.cards{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(270px,1fr));gap:18px}.card{background:#17212d;padding:15px;border-radius:10px}.caption{font-size:14px;color:#aebfd2}.thumbs{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(6,1fr);gap:9px}.thumbs button{padding:0;overflow:hidden;text-align:left}.thumbs img{width:100%;aspect-ratio:4/3;object-fit:fill;display:block}.thumbs span{padding:5px;display:block;font-size:11px}@media(max-width:700px){body{padding:14px}.thumbs{grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr)}td,th{padding:6px;font-size:13px}}
</style><h1>Sidewinder: terrain appraisal</h1><p>A terrain-only simplification, inspected through 24 repeatable single-player photos. Original baseline captures are reused from the identical route; all candidate captures are new. Visibility culling is disabled in both versions. This is an appraisal candidate; the accepted asset bank and release ROM remain in place.</p>
<div id="perf"></div>
<h2>Matched photos</h2><p>Twelve short walks from authored starts cover both base approaches, canyon bends, upper passes and base ramps. Each frame replays the production movement/collision tick from reset, then freezes at tick 90 or 180. Odd-numbered frames are crouched; two bend frames catch a descent and explicitly record grounded=false.</p>
<div class="tools"><button id="prev">←</button><select id="photo"></select><button id="next">→</button><span id="count"></span></div>
<div class="tools" id="modes"><button data-mode="before">Before</button><button data-mode="after">After</button><button data-mode="split" class="active">Wipe</button><button data-mode="diff">Difference</button></div>
<div class="tools"><label>Wipe <input id="wipe" type="range" min="0" max="100" value="50"></label><label>Difference threshold <input id="threshold" type="range" min="0" max="64" value="0"> <span id="thresholdValue">0</span>/255</label><label>Gain <input id="gain" type="range" min="1" max="16" value="4"> <span id="gainValue">4</span>×</label><label><input id="heat" type="checkbox"> Heat overlay</label></div>
<div class="frame"><img id="before" alt="Original terrain"><img id="after" class="top" alt="Simplified terrain"><canvas id="diff" class="hidden" width="640" height="240"></canvas><div id="divider" class="divider"></div></div>
<p id="pixelStats" class="caption"></p><p class="caption">Images are embedded so the pixel filter also works directly from a local file. Native Ares framebuffer captures are 640×240 samples, shown at the N64's 4:3 display aspect. Difference uses the maximum absolute RGB channel change to select samples, then displays amplified RGB differences or a heat overlay. Threshold 0 shows every change. Pose metadata starts at row 195; row 194 is retained in the scene check because the video filter blends the scene/panel boundary. Keyboard: ←/→ photos, B before, A after, S wipe, D difference.</p>
<pre id="pose"></pre><div class="tools"><a id="beforeDownload">Original PNG</a><a id="afterDownload">Candidate PNG</a><a id="beforeROM">Original fixture ROM (8 MiB)</a><a id="afterROM">Candidate fixture ROM (8 MiB)</a></div>
<div class="thumbs" id="thumbs"></div>
<h2>What changed, and what was protected</h2>__GEOMETRY__
<p>Walking paths retain the original collision surfaces. All 24 host walk/player states are byte-identical, and all 24 native pose strips preserve every compared pixel. This establishes reproducibility and mechanical path preservation; visual alignment is still for appraisal. Surface deviation checks sample vertices, edge midpoints and centroids in both directions; they are not a continuous mathematical bound.</p>
<p><a href="path-protection.json">Walking-surface protection proof</a> · <a href="validation.json">All verification results</a> · <a href="../n64-sidewinder-photography/comparison.html">Earlier conservative appraisal</a></p><p id="validation"></p><p><a href="sidewinder-appraisal.blend">Blender review scene</a> · <a href="terrain-candidate.json">Blender candidate and trial results</a> · <a href="packing-report.json">Packing/protection proof</a> · <a href="before-census/poses.json">Exact recorded states</a> · <a href="before-census/cameras.csv">Before submission counts</a> · <a href="after-census/cameras.csv">After submission counts</a> · <a href="pixel-comparisons.json">Pixel census</a> · <a href="timing.json">Timing records</a> · <a href="rdp-validation-native.png">Native RDP validation</a></p>
<script>const DATA=__DATA__;const $=id=>document.getElementById(id);let index=0,mode='split',generation=0;const poses=DATA.poses;
for(const p of poses){const o=document.createElement('option');o.value=p.photo;o.textContent=String(p.photo).padStart(2,'0')+' — '+p.label+(p.crouched?' / crouched':' / standing');$('photo').append(o);const b=document.createElement('button');const im=document.createElement('img');im.src=DATA.images.after[p.photo];im.alt=p.label;const s=document.createElement('span');s.textContent=String(p.photo).padStart(2,'0')+' '+p.label;b.append(im,s);b.onclick=()=>select(p.photo);$('thumbs').append(b);}
function setMode(m){mode=m;for(const b of $('modes').children)b.classList.toggle('active',b.dataset.mode===m);$('before').classList.toggle('hidden',m==='after'||m==='diff');$('after').classList.toggle('hidden',m==='before'||m==='diff');$('after').classList.toggle('top',m==='split');$('diff').classList.toggle('hidden',m!=='diff');$('divider').classList.toggle('hidden',m!=='split');filter();}
function filter(){const threshold=+$('threshold').value,gain=+$('gain').value;$('thresholdValue').textContent=threshold;$('gainValue').textContent=gain;const cut=+$('wipe').value;$('after').style.clipPath=mode==='split'?'inset(0 '+(100-cut)+'% 0 0)':'none';$('divider').style.left=cut+'%';if(!$('before').complete||!$('after').complete||!$('before').naturalWidth||!$('after').naturalWidth)return;const c=document.createElement('canvas');c.width=640;c.height=240;const x=c.getContext('2d',{willReadFrequently:true});x.drawImage($('before'),0,0);const a=x.getImageData(0,0,640,240);x.drawImage($('after'),0,0);const b=x.getImageData(0,0,640,240);const out=x.createImageData(640,240);let changed=0;for(let i=0;i<a.data.length;i+=4){const r=Math.abs(a.data[i]-b.data[i]),g=Math.abs(a.data[i+1]-b.data[i+1]),bl=Math.abs(a.data[i+2]-b.data[i+2]),v=Math.max(r,g,bl),scene=i/4<640*195,on=v>threshold&&scene;if(on)changed++;if($('heat').checked){out.data[i]=on?255:a.data[i]*.22;out.data[i+1]=on?Math.min(255,v*gain*2):a.data[i+1]*.22;out.data[i+2]=on?0:a.data[i+2]*.22;}else{out.data[i]=on?Math.min(255,r*gain):0;out.data[i+1]=on?Math.min(255,g*gain):0;out.data[i+2]=on?Math.min(255,bl*gain):0;}out.data[i+3]=255;}const context=$('diff').getContext('2d');context.putImageData(out,0,0);$('pixelStats').textContent=changed.toLocaleString()+' / '+(640*195).toLocaleString()+' scene samples exceed '+threshold+'/255 ('+(changed/(640*195)*100).toFixed(2)+'%). Pose metadata: 0 changed samples.';}
async function select(n){index=(n+poses.length)%poses.length;$('photo').value=index;$('count').textContent=(index+1)+' / '+poses.length;const p=poses[index],id=String(index).padStart(2,'0');const current=++generation;const paths=['photos/before/'+id+'-native.png','photos/after/'+id+'-native.png'];await Promise.all(paths.map((src,i)=>new Promise((resolve,reject)=>{const im=$(i?'after':'before');im.onload=resolve;im.onerror=reject;im.src=DATA.images[i?'after':'before'][index];})));if(current!==generation)return;const precise={...p};delete precise.player_bytes_hex;$('pose').textContent=JSON.stringify({coordinate_system:'N64 world: X, up, Z; radians for yaw/pitch',...precise,fov_radians:1.08,players:1,simulation_hz:30,framebuffer:[320,240],reconstruction:'Reset -> authored start -> photo_tour.h input ticks -> freeze; full player bytes in poses.json'},null,2);$('beforeDownload').href=paths[0];$('afterDownload').href=paths[1];$('beforeROM').href='photo-roms/before/'+id+'.z64';$('afterROM').href='photo-roms/after/'+id+'.z64';filter();}
$('prev').onclick=()=>select(index-1);$('next').onclick=()=>select(index+1);$('photo').onchange=()=>select(+$('photo').value);for(const b of $('modes').children)b.onclick=()=>setMode(b.dataset.mode);for(const id of ['threshold','gain','heat','wipe'])$(id).oninput=filter;document.onkeydown=e=>{if(e.target.tagName==='INPUT'||e.target.tagName==='SELECT')return;const m={b:'before',a:'after',s:'split',d:'diff'};if(m[e.key])setMode(m[e.key]);if(e.key==='ArrowLeft')select(index-1);if(e.key==='ArrowRight')select(index+1);};
const timing=DATA.timing;let rows='';for(const route of ['one','four']){const r=timing.filter(x=>x.route===route);if(!r.length)continue;const a=r.find(x=>x.label==='baseline'),b=r.find(x=>x.label==='candidate');if(a&&b)rows+='<tr><td>'+(route==='one'?'Single-player walking route':'Four-player production replay')+'</td><td>'+a.fps+' → '+b.fps+'</td><td>'+((b.poses/b.sample_ms)/(a.poses/a.sample_ms)*100-100).toFixed(2)+'%</td><td>'+a.p95_ms+' → '+b.p95_ms+' ms</td><td>'+a.max_ms+' → '+b.max_ms+' ms</td></tr>';}
$('perf').innerHTML='<h2>Quiet matched performance</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Route</th><th>Fresh-pose FPS</th><th>Pose-rate change</th><th>P95 interval</th><th>Maximum interval</th></tr></thead><tbody>'+rows+'</tbody></table><p>75-second Ares NTSC samples after one-second warmup, 8 MiB, LTO, three surfaces, 32 KiB queues. Baseline/candidate/baseline/candidate repeats; no live debug overlay or concurrent builds/tests. The single-player route uses ordinary presentation and can redraw a pose; the fresh-pose counter excludes those duplicate flips. The four-player route uses the maintained two-retrace pacing. __FLIPS__ These are separate workloads, not a direct comparison of player counts.</p><div class="cards">'+timing.map(x=>'<div class="card"><b>'+x.route+' player — '+x.label+'</b><p>'+x.poses+' fresh poses / '+x.sample_ms+' ms; '+x.fps+' FPS; free heap '+x.free_kib+' KiB.</p><a href="'+x.screenshot+'">Native result screenshot</a></div>').join('')+'</div>';
$('validation').textContent='Native four-camera source-start inspection: zero RDP errors and warnings, with 8 KiB validation queues. Repeated timing and sampled photos do not establish physical-console or exhaustive camera acceptance. Ares Expansion Pak/defocus preferences '+(DATA.settings_restored?'have been restored.':'will be restored after the run.');select(0);
</script></html>'''

def main():
    data={'images':{phase:['data:image/png;base64,'+base64.b64encode((OUT/f'photos/{phase}/{i:02}-native.png').read_bytes()).decode() for i in range(24)] for phase in ('before','after')},'poses':json.loads((OUT/'before-census/poses.json').read_text()),
          'timing':json.loads((OUT/'timing.json').read_text()) if (OUT/'timing.json').exists() else [],
          'settings_restored':(OUT/'ares-settings-restored.json').exists()}
    packing=json.loads((OUT/'packing-report.json').read_text())
    before=json.loads((OUT/'before-census/results.json').read_text());after=json.loads((OUT/'after-census/results.json').read_text())
    four=json.loads((OUT/'four-camera-results.json').read_text())
    cards=''
    for r in packing['blender_report']:
        error=r['attempts'][-1]['sampled_max_surface_error']
        cards+=f"<div class='card'><b>{r['name']}</b><p>{r['source_triangles']:,} → {r['candidate_triangles']:,} triangles. {r['pinned_vertices']:,} pinned vertices retain their coordinates. Maximum sampled bidirectional surface deviation: {error:.4f} world units.</p></div>"
    geometry="<div class='cards'>"+cards+"<div class='card'><b>Exact protection</b><p>Ice, architecture and scenery: 383 render batches preserve vertex bytes, local indices, bounds and relative order. All 20 non-render sections, including collision, are byte-identical. A no-change packing control reproduces the complete accepted bank.</p></div></div>"
    geometry+=f"<p>Across these 24 frozen views, mean submitted world vertex loads fall from {before['vertices']:,.1f} to {after['vertices']:,.1f} ({100*(1-after['vertices']/before['vertices']):.1f}%); world triangles fall from {before['triangles']:,.1f} to {after['triangles']:,.1f} ({100*(1-after['triangles']/before['triangles']):.1f}%). Total map render triangles: 15,635 → {packing['triangles']:,}; paired vertex loads: 22,564 → {packing['vertices']:,}; batches: 498 → {packing['chunks']}. Terrain seams stay pinned. Flatter cliff faces have additional pinned vertices; snow receives a tighter shape limit than steep rock. Lighting/texture interpolation and cliff faceting remain for visual appraisal.</p>"
    geometry+=f"<p>The four-player census matches 17 ticks × four cameras: mean world vertex loads {four['before']['vertices']:,.1f} → {four['after']['vertices']:,.1f}, triangles {four['before']['triangles']:,.1f} → {four['after']['triangles']:,.1f}, batches {four['before']['chunks']:.1f} → {four['after']['chunks']:.1f}. Every camera position, alive state and zoom state matches. Individual views can gain geometry after repacking. <a href='four-cameras.csv'>Matched records</a> · <a href='four-camera-results.json'>Summary</a>. Dynamic models are outside both world censuses.</p>"
    one=[r for r in data['timing'] if r['route']=='one']
    flips=''
    if one:
        a=next(r for r in one if r['label']=='baseline');b=next(r for r in one if r['label']=='candidate')
        flips=f"Single-player buffer flips {a['flips']:,}→{b['flips']:,}; duplicate-pose flips {a['duplicates']:,}→{b['duplicates']:,}. The simulation runs at 30 Hz."
    html=HTML.replace('__GEOMETRY__',geometry).replace('__FLIPS__',flips).replace('__DATA__',json.dumps(data,separators=(',',':')))
    (OUT/'comparison.html').write_text(html)
    (OUT/'report-script.js').write_text(html.split('<script>')[1].split('</script>')[0])
    print(OUT/'comparison.html')
if __name__=='__main__':
    import argparse
    parser=argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__);parser.add_argument('--output',type=Path,default=OUT);args=parser.parse_args();OUT=args.output.resolve();main()
